1. SCOPE

  This license covers the OROTP "core" — the source-available
  parts of the OROTP project that are not independently licensed
  under MIT. As of this version, the core comprises:

    - apps/server          (the Fastify API server, /admin
                            dashboard, hosted verification page,
                            webhook delivery worker, multi-receiver
                            routing, WebAuthn backend, and any
                            related core service code)
    - apps/gsm-gateway     (the Python USB-modem inbound SMS
                            gateway)
    - any future top-level "apps/*" service component the upstream
      project explicitly designates as core

  The MIT-licensed SDKs, UI components, CLI, and examples are NOT
  covered by this license. See LICENSE-MIT and Section 8 below.


2. DEFINITIONS

  "Software" means any source file in this repository covered by
  this license, plus any derivative work containing a substantive
  portion of such source.

  "OROTP Core Service" means a deployment of the Software (or any
  derivative) that performs reverse-OTP / SMS verification for
  end users, applications, or third parties.

  "Commercial Use" means any operation of an OROTP Core Service
  where any party receives monetary or other in-kind consideration
  in exchange for access to, hosting of, or operation of that
  service. Examples (non-exhaustive):

    - Charging end users to receive verifications.
    - Charging developers, customers, or organizations a fee, a
      subscription, a per-call price, or any other consideration
      to call OROTP-backed APIs.
    - Bundling the Software inside a paid product where the
      verification capability is a marketed or load-bearing
      feature.
    - Offering an OROTP Core Service under a different brand name
      to paying customers.

  "You" means the natural person or legal entity exercising
  rights under this license.


3. PERMISSIONS GRANTED FREE OF CHARGE

  Subject to the conditions in Section 5, You may, free of charge:

  (a) Read, study, audit, and learn from the Software.
  (b) Modify the Software for any of the uses listed in (c)–(g).
  (c) Run the Software for personal use.
  (d) Run the Software for educational, academic, or research use.
  (e) Run the Software for charitable, humanitarian, or non-profit
      use, including operating an OROTP Core Service whose end
      users are not charged by any party for verifications and
      where the operating organization is not paid by any third
      party for the operation of that service.
  (f) Run the Software inside a single organization for that
      organization's own internal verification needs ("Internal
      Use"), provided the verifications are not exposed as a paid
      product, paid platform feature, or paid API to third
      parties.
  (g) Distribute the Software in source form, with all of the
      terms of this license preserved.
  (h) Submit modifications back to the upstream OROTP repository
      as contributions.


